// Title: Linux Base64 Encoded Pipe to Shell
// Sigma ID: ba592c6d-6888-43c3-b8c6-689b8fe47337
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: pH-T (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-26 | Modified: 2023-06-16
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1140
// Description: Detects suspicious process command line that uses base64 encoded input for execution with a
//   shell
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities
// References:
//   - https://github.com/arget13/DDexec
//   - https://www.mandiant.com/resources/blog/barracuda-esg-exploited-globally
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_base64_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "base64 " and ((ProcessCommandLine contains "| bash " or ProcessCommandLine contains "| sh " or ProcessCommandLine contains "|bash " or ProcessCommandLine contains "|sh ") or (ProcessCommandLine endswith " |sh" or ProcessCommandLine endswith "| bash" or ProcessCommandLine endswith "| sh" or ProcessCommandLine endswith "|bash"))
